vendor/libraw/ - LibRaw for the browser (used by Photo Lab to open camera RAW files)
===================================================================================

The four program files here are the UNMODIFIED "dist" files of the npm package
libraw-wasm 1.6.0 (https://www.npmjs.com/package/libraw-wasm,
source: https://github.com/ybouane/LibRaw-Wasm, tag v1.6.0):

  index.js     the small module that starts the worker
               sha256 3eb710aa5473c58c3b9dec74457b2ad2095d15b9a6df0056c96a3a011b720ca6
  worker.js    the module worker + Emscripten glue
               sha256 af074781439ddf9c47fcbd3b3f115049ab884fdf61ec49ab358f28a8c42a4d4c
  libraw.js    Emscripten glue (thread helper)
               sha256 e23952fca5b268550af1f84619af5c0c035e5db3bde0e4d5a20300f1614a9487
  libraw.wasm  LibRaw 0.22.1 + Little-CMS 2.19.1 + libjpeg (Emscripten port),
               compiled to WebAssembly by the package's own build
               sha256 8947f7e668e488461c3e9defe7007583aa8477b4886aa603b36b407f2f0846ff

They are kept as separate files and loaded only when a RAW file is opened, so
anyone can replace them with their own build of the same libraries (the
interface is index.js's LibRaw class: open, metadata, imageData). The package's
source maps are left out; nothing else is changed.

